														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-1751437">
									

<p>No the rules didn't change. If someone had been in a location on the periphery of the new area, they'd've been able to leave. But the people deeper in the affected area were surrounded by newly unapproachable areas. As for the inability to be rescued from the air, I'm basing at least part of this SCP on the psychological concept of &quot;boundary events.&quot; Very basically, the mind uses physical boundaries as signs to end/create discrete purely mental boundaries as well. This is a leading hypothesis for why it's so easy to walk into a new room and completely forget why you went in there: The mind &quot;closed&quot; the thought when you crossed through the doorway and &quot;started&quot; a new one.</p>
<p>In the case of this SCP, <em>something</em> considered arbitrary boundaries as inviolate, separating discrete physical spaces. And those boundaries can be something like &quot;the telephone poles overhead define a discrete airspace location&quot; which the pedestrian now can't approach.</p>

							</div>

